      "writtenOn": "2025-11-17T08:42:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glslang/commit/d1888f83f6038004d62c67bc19b2b2f180c0219c seems to be adding conservative depth layout qualifiers support to glslang without `GL_EXT_conservative_depth` since it\u0027s using `#version 420 core`.\nI\u0027ve forced generating `#version 420 core` GLSL shaders (instead of `#version 310 es`) but I now got the following error:\n\n```\nError parsing GLSL shader:\nERROR: 0:11: \u0027location qualifier on uniform or buffer\u0027 : not supported for this version or the enabled extensions \nERROR: 1 compilation errors.  No code generated.\n```\n\nDoes that I mean I\u0027m out of luck for this kind of tests like you suggested?\n\n@cwallez@chromium.org Any thoughts on this?",
