      "writtenOn": "2025-11-17T10:57:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s try with https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glslang/pull/4096 and see how people react to it. Note that with this patch, the following code is now valid:\n\n```\n#version 300 es\n#extension GL_EXT_spirv_intrinsics: require\n#extension GL_EXT_conservative_depth: require\nlayout (depth_any) out highp float gl_FragDepth;\nvoid main() {\n    gl_FragDepth \u003d 1.0;\n}\n```\n\nNote that I had to enable also `GL_EXT_spirv_intrinsics` to avoid the following error. I wonder if that\u0027s okay...\n\n```\nERROR: 0:3: \u0027gl_FragDepth\u0027 : identifiers starting with \"gl_\" are reserved \nERROR: 1 compilation errors.  No code generated.\n```",
